        "annotations": [
          {
            "id": "an1",
            "kind": "label",
            "x": 0,
            "y": -14.6,
            "text": "A step-down transformer: 120 V~ in, 12 V~ out, and what a load takes off it"
          },
          {
            "id": "an2",
            "kind": "label",
            "x": 0,
            "y": -12.8,
            "text": "Turn on Settings ▸ Spice Lite and Run. Two coils on one core, 10 turns to 1: the",
            "color": "#808080"
          },
          {
            "id": "an3",
            "kind": "label",
            "x": 0,
            "y": -11,
            "text": "secondary swings ±17 V for the primary's ±170 V (see the analyzer). It is not a",
            "color": "#808080"
          },
          {
            "id": "an4",
            "kind": "label",
            "x": 0,
            "y": -9.2,
            "text": "perfect ratio — 0.6 Ω of secondary winding, 40 Ω of primary and a 1 % leakage",
            "color": "#808080"
          },
          {
            "id": "an5",
            "kind": "label",
            "x": 0,
            "y": -7.4,
            "text": "(coupling 0.99) sit in series with whatever it feeds. Slide the switch to add",
            "color": "#808080"
          },
          {
            "id": "an6",
            "kind": "label",
            "x": 0,
            "y": -5.6,
            "text": "10 Ω beside the 100 Ω: the secondary sags about a tenth. Open the transformer's",
            "color": "#808080"
          },
          {
            "id": "an7",
            "kind": "label",
            "x": 0,
            "y": -3.8,
            "text": "Properties and try Rating ▸ Custom… — the turns, the windings, the coupling.",
            "color": "#808080"
          }
        ],
